.TH CUBE-PROMPTS-STUDIO 1 "October 2026" "Cube Prompts" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cube-prompts-studio \- local prompt library and AI comparison workbench
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cube-prompts-studio
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Organize AI prompts, fill template variables, save revisions, export libraries,
and compare responses from supported providers or local Ollama models.
The library and editor work without an Internet connection.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
Display available options and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Display the application version and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-page " PAGE"
Start on library, run, templates, history, export, or settings.
.TP
.BI \-\-screenshot " FILE"
Render a preview PNG and exit. Requires a graphical display.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/cube-prompts/prompts.db
SQLite library, defaulting to ~/.local/share/cube-prompts/prompts.db.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cube-prompts/settings.json
Application settings, defaulting to ~/.config/cube-prompts/settings.json.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cube-prompts/credentials.json
Private credential fallback when no supported OS keyring is available.
.SH NOTES
The standalone package coexists with Whitecube Desktop. Its command is
cube-prompts-studio, while Whitecube's command remains cube-prompts.
Both use the same per-user library. Removing the package preserves user data.
